  playerLines:
  - Woah
  - What's with these wacky symbols?
  - I can assign any value I want to these variables?
  - <i>hmm...</i>
  - <i>So I can first assign a number to a variable</i>
  - <i>Then I can use operations on this variable</i>
  - <i>Even time can be represented as a variable</i>
  NPCLines:
  - This is the greek alphabet, used extensively in all of science
  - And most scientists aren't greek
  - The Greek alphabet was created around 1000 BCE and is the ancestor of all modern
    European alphabets
  - These symbols are the building blocks of algebra
  - These symbols can denote numbers and operations can be applied on these variables
  - "Fran\xE7ois Vi\xE8te introduced the concept of the modern variable in the late
    16th century"
  - No, remember only a number can be used as a variable
  - Operations are then performed on this number
